## Findings

- **[P1] Schema-declared secrets can leak into workflow artifacts.** [`_portable_settings()`](/D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/studio/workflows/adapters/common.py:156) calls `portable_provider_settings()` without the provider schema. Consequently, a secret declared solely through `ui.type: "password"`—for example `license_code`—is treated as portable unless its name also matches the secret regex. `provider_run_options()` then forwards it into legacy option dictionaries that can be persisted in job metadata. A direct probe returned `{'license_code': 'TOPSECRET', ...}`. Pass the schema into portable-settings filtering and filter the merged result against both secret properties and known properties.

- **[P1] Phase 12.5’s central extensibility gate is not actually satisfied.** The new test explicitly excludes execution through `tts.generate` and `storyboard.generate` because their adapters still branch through legacy implementations ([test declaration](/D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/tests/test_provider_extensibility.py:22)). Instead, the fixture providers are invoked directly through `boundary.invoke()` or `instance.submit()`. In production, the nodes still call `_step_tts` and `_step_storyboard` ([TTS adapter](/D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/studio/workflows/adapters/tts.py:26), [Storyboard adapter](/D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/studio/workflows/adapters/storyboard.py:97)), so selecting either fixture on the existing generic node does not execute that provider. This contradicts the step’s requirement that every execution shape complete catalog → settings → node validation → node execution; Phase 12 should not be marked closed yet.

- **[P2] Switching between provider-backed node types can show the previous domain’s providers.** `ConfigField` captures `props.field.options_source` once during setup ([ConfigField.vue](/D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/frontend/src/features/workflow/components/ConfigField.vue:35)), while the inspector keys fields only by `field.name` ([NodeInspector.vue](/D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/frontend/src/features/workflow/components/NodeInspector.vue:199)). Because all converted nodes use `provider_id`, Vue reuses the component when moving, for example, from Story Generator to TTS. Its source remains `script_providers`, so the TTS node displays and can save a script provider. Include the node/type or option source in the key, or make the option-source subscription reactive.

- **[P2] A transient schema request failure is permanently cached as “no options.”** `loadProviderSchema()` converts every API/network error to `null` and stores it in the schema cache ([providerCatalog.js](/D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/frontend/src/features/providers/stores/providerCatalog.js:352)). The inspector then reports that the provider has no per-run options, provides no error or retry, and will not refetch until the catalog version changes or the page reloads. Only a confirmed schema-less response should cache `null`; request failures should remain distinguishable and retryable.

